RedShipBlueShip is licensed under the MIT License, reproduced in full below.

SCOPE. The MIT grant below covers RedShipBlueShip's OWN code, documentation and
build glue only. Concretely, that is:

  * src/common/**            (unified lifecycle, context, entrance, menu,
                              netplay, shared-resource and test code)
  * rsbs/**                  (the redship entry point)
  * CMake/**                 (this project's build configuration, except the
                              vendored automate-vcpkg.cmake noted below)
  * tools/**, scripts/**     (this project's audit and packaging scripts)
  * docs/**, CLAUDE.md, README.md, this file
  * the single-executable glue added to the vendored game trees - the
    *SingleExe* translation units under games/oot/** and games/mm/**, the
    RedShipBlueShip test translation units alongside them, and the changes
    made inside SINGLE_EXECUTABLE_BUILD guards

It does NOT cover, and does not purport to relicense:

  * games/oot/**  - the vendored Ship of Harkinian tree
  * games/mm/**   - the vendored 2Ship2Harkinian tree
  * libultraship/, ZAPDTR/, OTRExporter/ - submodules with their own LICENSE
  * CMake/automate-vcpkg.cmake - MIT, Copyright (c) 2019 REGoth-project
  * any other third-party code, font or data file in the tree or fetched at
    build time

Those components keep their own licenses. THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md inventories
every one of them, with the license, the copyright line, the upstream URL, the
license elected where the upstream offers a choice, and the one remaining
component whose license status is unresolved. Read it before redistributing a
build. The license texts that must travel with a component are in the tree
beside it: games/mm/LICENSE (CC0-1.0, the vendored MM port) and
games/{oot,mm}/assets/custom/fonts/OFL.txt (SIL Open Font License 1.1, the
fonts).

No copyrighted Nintendo asset is included in this repository. RedShipBlueShip
extracts assets at build time from original Ocarina of Time and Majora's Mask
ROMs that you must supply yourself.

